IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ks-tanf`

-- Kansas TANF -- the seat of the applicant (the parent or relative applying for, or receiving, TANF for a child).
--
-- "Is my child a dependent child? Do we meet the general requirements? Have we used up the time limit? How many hours a
-- week must we work? How long is my penalty? What is the most TANF pays a family our size in our county?" Every answer is
-- built from the rules in ks-tanf.l4.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Kansas TANF -- my questions`

§§ `Who can get TANF`

@export Is this child a "dependent child" for Kansas TANF (K.S.A. 39-702(g))?
GIVEN `the child's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The child's age in whole years
      `the child is a full-time secondary school student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the child is 18: whether they are a full-time student in high school or an equivalent program
      `the child lives with a relative in that relative's home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child lives with a parent or other relative (grandparent, aunt, uncle, cousin, sibling, or their spouses or former spouses) in a home that relative maintains
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this child a dependent child` IF
    `is a dependent child` `the child's age` `the child is a full-time secondary school student` `the child lives with a relative in that relative's home`

@export Do I meet Kansas's general requirements for public assistance (K.S.A. 39-709(a))?
GIVEN `the department finds our income or resources insufficient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the department for children and families has found your family's income and resources insufficient for a reasonable subsistence (your spouse's or cohabiting partner's income counts too; one vehicle is exempt)
      `I am a citizen or lawfully admitted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a US citizen or an alien lawfully admitted to the United States
      `I live in Kansas` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you reside in Kansas
      `I quit a job voluntarily or was fired for gross misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you voluntarily quit employment, or were fired for gross misconduct
      `I am a fugitive from justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a fugitive from justice for a felony conviction or charge, or for violating probation or parole
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the general requirements` IF
    `meets the 39-709(a) general requirements` (`General eligibility facts` WITH
        `income or resources are insufficient, as the secretary determines` IS `the department finds our income or resources insufficient`
        `a citizen or an alien lawfully admitted` IS `I am a citizen or lawfully admitted`
        `resides in Kansas` IS `I live in Kansas`
        `voluntarily quit employment, or was fired for gross misconduct` IS `I quit a job voluntarily or was fired for gross misconduct`
        `a fugitive from justice for a felony, or a probation or parole violation` IS `I am a fugitive from justice`)

@export Is our family still within the Kansas TANF time limit (K.S.A. 39-709(b)(3))?
GIVEN `the most months any adult in our family has had TANF` IS A NUMBER @desc The largest number of calendar months, since October 1996, that any adult in your family group has received TANF, in Kansas or any other state
      `our hardship` IS A `Hardship` @desc Which hardship, if any, applies to you
      `the secretary granted a hardship extension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the secretary has granted your family a hardship extension
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are we within the time limit` IF
    `is within the time limit` `the most months any adult in our family has had TANF` `our hardship` `the secretary granted a hardship extension`

-- Only for an applicant or recipient under 18 who has a child or is pregnant.
@export I am under 18, unmarried, and have a child or am pregnant: can a TANF grant be paid for me where I live (K.S.A. 39-7,124)?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age
      `I have ever been married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have ever married
      `I have a child or am pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a child or are pregnant
      `I live with a parent, guardian or adult relative, or in supervised housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live with a parent, legal guardian or other adult relative, or in a foster home, maternity home or other adult-supervised arrangement
      `an exception applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have no living parent or guardian (or their whereabouts are unknown), the state has found your or your child's health or safety would be at risk, or you lived apart from your parent or guardian for at least a year before the birth or your application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a grant be paid for me as a minor parent` IF
    NOT (`the 39-7,124 bar applies` `my age` `I have ever been married` `I have a child or am pregnant` `I live with a parent, guardian or adult relative, or in supervised housing` `an exception applies to me`)

§§ `Work requirements`

@export Must I complete a module of the TANF work program assessment while my application is processed (K.S.A. 39-709(b)(5), (6))?
GIVEN `my good cause` IS A `Good cause for the assessment` @desc Which good cause, if any, you have
      `I am a caretaker not otherwise eligible, or I receive SSI` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an adult not otherwise eligible for TANF (an ineligible alien, a relative or non-relative caretaker, or receiving SSI)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I complete an assessment module` IF
    `must complete a module of the work program assessment` `my good cause` `I am a caretaker not otherwise eligible, or I receive SSI`

@export How many hours a week, in total, must our household take part in TANF work activities (K.S.A. 39-709(b)(8)(B))?
GIVEN `we are a two-parent household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether two parents live in the household
      `our youngest child is under six` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the youngest child is under six years old
      `we get child care paid by the department` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the department for children and families pays for your child care
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many hours a week must we take part` MEANS
    (`required weekly participation` `we are a two-parent household` `our youngest child is under six` `we get child care paid by the department`)'s `total hours`

@export Of those hours, how many must be in primary work components such as employment, job search or work experience (K.S.A. 39-709(b)(8)(B), (C))?
GIVEN `we are a two-parent household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether two parents live in the household
      `our youngest child is under six` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the youngest child is under six years old
      `we get child care paid by the department` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the department for children and families pays for your child care
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many hours must be primary` MEANS
    (`required weekly participation` `we are a two-parent household` `our youngest child is under six` `we get child care paid by the department`)'s `primary hours`

-- Only for a parent or caretaker of a new baby.
@export Am I exempt from TANF work activities because I am caring for a baby (K.S.A. 39-709(b)(8)(D))?
GIVEN `I personally care for a child under three months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you personally care for a child in your TANF household who is under three months old
      `the child was born very premature, seriously ill or disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child was born significantly premature, with serious medical conditions or with a disability, as the secretary defines
      `two parents live in our home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether two parents are in the home and the household meets the two-parent definition
      `another adult at home can care for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another parent or caretaker in the home is available, capable and suitable to provide the care
      `I am 19 or younger without a diploma` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are 19 or younger, pregnant or a parent, and without a high school diploma or equivalent
      `I am assigned to substance use treatment as my work activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your work participation activity is for a substance use disorder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I exempt for a young child` IF
    `is exempt from work participation for a young child` `I personally care for a child under three months` `the child was born very premature, seriously ill or disabled` `two parents live in our home` `another adult at home can care for the child` `I am 19 or younger without a diploma` `I am assigned to substance use treatment as my work activity`

-- Only after a finding of non-cooperation with work programs or child support services.
@export For how many months am I ineligible for TANF after this penalty for not cooperating with work programs or child support services (K.S.A. 39-709(b)(8)(G), (9))?
GIVEN `which penalty this is` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for a first penalty, 2 for a second, 3 for a third, 4 or more for a fourth or later
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How long is my TANF penalty` MEANS `months of ineligibility for non-cooperation` `which penalty this is`

§§ `How much`

@export What is the TANF payment standard, the most a family our size in our county can receive each month before income is counted (K.A.R. 30-4-100, 30-4-101)?
GIVEN `the number of persons in our assistance plan` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your TANF assistance plan
      `our county` IS A STRING @desc The Kansas county you live in, for example "Sedgwick" or "Johnson"
      `others outside the plan live with us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone not in your assistance plan lives in your home (answer no if the only such person is an SSI recipient whose SSI is reduced by one-third, a commercial landlord or tenant, or if you live in commercial board and room or a publicly or charitably funded shelter or facility)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is our TANF payment standard` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the shelter group of` `our county`
    WHEN JUST g THEN JUST (`the TANF payment standard` `the number of persons in our assistance plan` g `others outside the plan live with us`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@export How much of my monthly earnings is left to count after the $90 work expense and 40% work-and-earn disregard (K.S.A. 39-7,127)?
GIVEN `my gross monthly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your gross monthly earned income
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my earnings counts` MEANS `earned income left after the 39-7,127 disregard` `my gross monthly earnings`
